- FACTOR removes prime factors ≤ B, perfect powers and primes. The surviving N has every prime factor > B
  and ω(N) ≥ 2. Then ω(N) ≤ log N/log B, so 2^{ω} ≤ exp(O((log N/log log N)^{1/2})) = L^{o(1)}
